<title>GERMANY: VW SAYS 1996 GROUP PROFIT DOUBLED.</title>
<headline>VW SAYS 1996 GROUP PROFIT DOUBLED.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group profit				 678     vs 336</p>
<p>    Parent profit				630     vs 410</p>
<p>    Group investment			   15,279  vs 13,072</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    10,853  vs 10,400</p>
<p>    Group sales				  100,123 vs 88,119</p>
<p>    Group vehicle deliveries (units)     3,994   vs 3,607</p>
<p>    Dividend per ordinary share		  9   vs 6 marks</p>
<p>    Dividend per preference share		10  vs 7 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - German carmaker Volkswagen AG said the dividend rise would be proposed by the management to the supervisory board which will decide whether to approve it on March 21. -- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
